The true border holds, and the road goes around the mill. Ashcombe keeps its wheel and its quarrels. #line:ending_true_around
The true border holds, and the road goes through the village. The mill comes down by midsummer. #line:ending_true_through
The steward's border is drawn. The abbey loses its meadows, and nobody can say why. #line:ending_forged
The steward is exposed before the whole fair, and leaves the valley before the evening. #line:ending_exposed
The border follows the path the villagers walk. Nobody is pleased, and nobody fights. #line:ending_walked
The hearing ends without a border. The quarrel goes on for another generation. #line:ending_failed
===

title: StoryNotes
act: All
location: Anywhere
scenario: The state of the story
style: note
---
Four acts. Act I is the village and its houses (child scenes), for two days. Act II is the castle (a separate scene), for one day, and the feast sends the cartographer back to the village and back. Act III is the mine (a separate scene with its levels as child scenes), for one shift, with the lamp oil as the clock. Act IV is the village again, with the fair (a child scene loaded by the story) and the hearing, which gives one of six endings.
===
